    <item>
      <title>AI WEEK x Startup Barreiro - Build Your Product with AI: 4-Hour Intensive Workshop</title>
      <link>https://luma.com/7yyocx0l?utm_source=adamastor.blog&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=rss_events_software-engineering</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">https://adamastor.blog/events#event-1279</guid>
      <pubDate>Tue, 22 Sep 2026 21:34:22 GMT</pubDate>
      <description>Walk in with an idea. Walk out with a working product you built yourself. No coding, no excuses, 4 hours.
You have had the idea for months. Maybe years. An app, a tool, a platform, the thing that would make your business run better or become a business on its own. And every time you get close, the same wall: &quot;I can&apos;t build it, and I can&apos;t afford someone who can.&quot;
That wall is gone. On 24 September, at Startup Barreiro, you will build it. Not watch it get built. Build it.
Official event of Lisbon</description>
      <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><img src="https://images.lumacdn.com/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=cover,dpr=1,anim=false,background=white,quality=75,width=800,height=420/event-social/27/f5ce41f8-3c44-4ac3-9fb3-30bddb20cd3f.png" alt="" style="max-width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:6px;"></p><p><strong>When:</strong> Thursday, 24 September 2026 at 18:30<br><strong>Where:</strong> Lisboa</p><p>Walk in with an idea. Walk out with a working product you built yourself. No coding, no excuses, 4 hours.<br>You have had the idea for months. Maybe years. An app, a tool, a platform, the thing that would make your business run better or become a business on its own. And every time you get close, the same wall: &quot;I can&apos;t build it, and I can&apos;t afford someone who can.&quot;<br>That wall is gone. On 24 September, at Startup Barreiro, you will build it. Not watch it get built. Build it.<br>Official event of Lisbon AI Week 2026. First edition in Margem Sul.<br>What makes this different<br>Most AI events are talks. Someone shows slides, you nod, you go home with nothing.<br>This is the opposite. From minute one you have your laptop open and your hands on real tools. I show you the method, you build your product, I stay in the room to unstick you the moment you get stuck. By the end, there is something on your screen that did not exist 4 hours earlier, and you made it.<br>Your guide (aka me, Alex Russo): 20+ years in tech, built products for Fortune 100 companies, 20,000+ entrepreneurs taught, and the person who has run this exact format to sold-out rooms in Lisbon.<br>How the 4 hours work<br>Phase 1, Foundation (60 to 90 min). Software architecture for non-technical entrepreneurs, made simple. We vote on one business idea from the room, turn it into a Product Requirements Document (PRD) and build it live in front of you, so you see every step of the method before you use it. Vibe coding all the way, with an eye on solid architecture.<br>Phase 2, Build Time (2.5 hours). Now it is your idea. Work alone or team up with people whose ideas complement yours, your choice. You build with the same tools and the same method, with me at your table for direct support and real-time problem solving.<br>Phase 3, Showcase (30 min). You present what you built, get feedback and next steps, and we celebrate it. Yes, you will have something to show.<br>What you walk away with<br>A working prototype of YOUR product, usable in your business from the next day<br>The complete AI-powered development workflow, so you can do it again without me<br>The PRD template I use, ready for your next projects<br>Access to every tool, template and resource used during the workshop<br>A room full of entrepreneurs who now know what you are building<br>Priority access to what comes next (you will find out on the day)<br>What your ticket includes<br>All premium AI development tools for the session. You do not pay for anything else.<br>Dinner, so you build through the evening without leaving the room<br>Take-home templates and guides<br>Recording of the key concepts for reference<br>The chance to pitch your idea to other entrepreneurs<br>This is for you if<br>You are an entrepreneur with an idea that has waited long enough<br>You run a business and want to test a concept before spending real money on it<br>You are a freelancer, consultant or creator who wants their own product<br>You are simply curious what AI can actually build today, done properly, not hyped<br>This is not for you if<br>You want to sit back and watch. This is hands-on building.<br>You cannot bring a laptop.<br>Before you come<br>Bring a laptop, charged. Everything else is set up together in the room, so we start building from minute one.<br>25 seats only, so I can be at every table. Previous editions in Lisbon sold out.<br>Your instructor<br>Alex Russo. Serial entrepreneur, community owner of Lisbon Entrepreneurs and Creators and VibeFounders Lisbon, and founder of VibeFounders, an applied AI and AI-native businesses incubator brand. 20+ years in tech including Fortune 100 product work. Lives in Portugal, on this side of the river. Passionate about making advanced technology usable by technical and non-technical entrepreneurs alike.<br>LinkedIn: /alessandro-russo-wym<br>Partners<br>Lisbon AI Week 2026. This workshop is an official event of Lisbon AI Week, the week of AI events across the city organized by Observador (lisbonaiweek.com). We are proud to be the one bringing it to Margem Sul.<br>Startup Barreiro and Município do Barreiro. Hosted at Startup Barreiro (https://www.startupbarreiro.pt/), the municipal business incubator of Barreiro, who opened their doors to make the first edition on this side of the river possible.<br>Venue and getting there<br>Startup Barreiro, Sala Rio Tejo. Parque Empresarial da Baía do Tejo (Quimiparque), Edifício 23, next to Jardim dos Franceses. Free parking on site.<br>From Lisbon: 20 minutes on the ferry from Terreiro do Paço to Barreiro.<br>Stop talking about your idea. Come build it.</p><p><a href="https://luma.com/7yyocx0l?utm_source=adamastor.blog&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=rss_events_software-engineering">View event details and RSVP →</a></p>]]></content:encoded>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>AI Hacker House: Equinox Edition</title>
      <link>https://luma.com/34od3n97?utm_source=adamastor.blog&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=rss_events_software-engineering</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">https://adamastor.blog/events#event-1255</guid>
      <pubDate>Mon, 14 Sep 2026 09:56:18 GMT</pubDate>
      <description>A full day of building with workshops, human mentors, and demos.
AI Hacker House is back with an in-person hacking sprint where builders of all backgrounds come together to build with AI, from first idea to working prototype.
Last edition sold out and 15 teams walked out with working projects by the end of the day. Now we&apos;re doing it again, bigger, and during Lisbon AI Week.
Sponsored by DeHouse, YLD and Blip.pt.

With Lisbon AI Week, Innovation X Hub by Porto Business School and Center for Resp</description>
      <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><img src="https://images.lumacdn.com/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=cover,dpr=1,anim=false,background=white,quality=75,width=800,height=420/event-social/sr/1963b3d2-b588-4f09-be53-30618769b89d.png" alt="" style="max-width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:6px;"></p><p><strong>When:</strong> Friday, 25 September 2026 at 10:00<br><strong>Where:</strong> Lisboa</p><p>A full day of building with workshops, human mentors, and demos.<br>AI Hacker House is back with an in-person hacking sprint where builders of all backgrounds come together to build with AI, from first idea to working prototype.<br>Last edition sold out and 15 teams walked out with working projects by the end of the day. Now we&apos;re doing it again, bigger, and during Lisbon AI Week.<br>Sponsored by DeHouse, YLD and Blip.pt.<br><br>With Lisbon AI Week, Innovation X Hub by Porto Business School and Center for Responsible AI as Community Partners.<br>Who&apos;s it for<br>Everyone. Developers, designers, marketers, sales, entrepreneurs, and anyone curious about AI. No experience required, no team required. Come solo or bring your crew.<br>The details<br>September 25, 2026<br>DeHouse Picoas, R. Tomás Ribeiro 65, Lisboa<br>Free registration, 100 spots available<br>Prizes for the best projects<br>Not sure if you should come?<br>This is your chance to push the boundaries of what autonomous agents can do, compete for sponsor challenges, and connect with humans building cool stuff.<br>More informations coming soon.</p><p><a href="https://luma.com/34od3n97?utm_source=adamastor.blog&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=rss_events_software-engineering">View event details and RSVP →</a></p>]]></content:encoded>
    </item>
